# asm2.hex1 -- rung 2 of the Omega seed chain: "names", a two-pass assembler whose instruction set is
# a readable text table. Written in hex1's language (rung 1: 8-digit words, ':c' labels, '@c' branch
# marks, '#' comments) and built by hex1: hex1.bin < asm2.hex1 > asm2.bin.
# Input language of asm2 (one statement per line, ';' starts a comment, words split by spaces/tabs/commas):
#   = name 0xBASE field...   table line: an instruction name, its fixed bits, then one field per operand:
#                            rP (register, 5 bits at bit P), iP.W (unsigned, W bits at P), sP.W (signed),
#                            lP.W (distance to a label in words, signed, W bits at P), a (ADR byte distance:
#                            low 2 bits at 29, the rest at 5..23). Width defaults to 5.
#   :name                    a label: the current output position in bytes
#   name operand...          an instruction from the table; registers x0..x30 w0..w30 xzr wzr sp wsp,
#                            numbers [-]decimal or [-]0x lower-case hex, labels by name (up to 16 characters)
#   .w number / .b number    one 32-bit little-endian word / one byte
# Errors print "asm2: line N: error E" on stderr and exit E: 1 read, 2 write, 3 unknown name, 4 too few
# operands, 5 extra words, 6 bad number, 7 bad register, 8 out of range, 9 unknown label, 10 label twice,
# 11 name twice, 12 bad table line, 13 word over 16 characters, 14 not 4-byte aligned, 15 unknown
# directive, 16 table/labels/output full.
# Memory (one mapping at 0x400000): table 0x500000 (1024 x 64 bytes: name 16, base 8, field count 8,
# 8 fields of kind/position/width), labels 0x510000 (8192 x 32 bytes: name 16, position 8), message
# buffer 0x5f0000, input 0x600000, output 0xe00000 (8 MiB).
#
# ---- ELF-64 file header, 16 words ----
